  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "伊斯蘭及中東政治經濟",
    "sub_ename": "ISLAM AND THE POLITICS AND ECONOMY IN THE MIDDLE EAST",
    "describe_ch": "中東地區的政治、宗教族群及經濟發展一直是國際政治的重要議題，且在地理上中東位於歐、亞、非三大洲的交匯處，具深具地緣政治及地緣經濟之戰略意義。中東政治經濟與伊斯蘭議題雖複雜卻具探索的吸引力，本課程希望藉由四大單元主題的授課內容、電影賞析及分組討論等方式，帶領同學認識伊斯蘭文化、伊朗及波斯灣王國的政治經濟發展、以巴衝突、葉門內戰等議題，提升學生的國際視野及思辨能力。",
    "describe_eh": "The politics, religions, ethnic groups, and economic developments of the Middle East have always been important issues in international politics. Geographically, the Middle East region is located at the crossroads of the three continents of Europe, Asia, and Africa, which has profound strategic significance in geopolitical and geo-economic aspects. Although the issues of the political economy and Islam in the Middle East are complex, they are also attractive to explore. This course hopes to lead students to understand Islamic culture, the political economy development of Iran, and the Persian Gulf kingdoms, the Israeli-Palestinian conflicts, Yemen’s civil war, and other issues, and to enhance students’ international vision and critical thinking ability, through the ways of the teaching content of the four major themes, film appreciation, and the group discussions.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
